<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Old Santiam Wagon Road</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:244-4: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="44.373619" lon="-122.004265"><ele>990.3</ele><name>Ikenick (Isaac Nickerson) Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:ikenick-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 246; book_elev_ft: 3280; quote: If turnout parking is not possible, park at Ikenick Sno-Park and ski north on the east leg of the Prairie View Loop</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.391400" lon="-122.009990"><ele>1003.0</ele><name>Leave the Prairie View east leg</name><desc>source: USFS EDW SNO-3561 PRAIRIE VIEW LOOP vertex where the east leg turns west, about 1.3 mi from the sno-park; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 246; quote: Ski about 1.3 miles, enter forest to the east, find a primitive road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.391890" lon="-122.005120"><ele>962.1</ele><name>Primitive road (USFS 2600726)</name><desc>source: USFS EDW road 2600726 vertex due east of the turn; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 246; quote: find a primitive road, and ski this north to Fish Lake</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.396480" lon="-122.004810"><ele>961.9</ele><name>Fish Lake (north end of road 2600726)</name><desc>source: north end of USFS road 2600726, by Fish Lake; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 246; quote: ski this north to Fish Lake and access to all the routes</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.394620" lon="-122.002680"><ele>960.3</ele><name>Highway crossing</name><desc>source: west end of USFS road 2600777 (spur to the McKenzie River Trail lot), about 400 yd south of Fish Lake; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 246; quote: ski south from Fish Lake along the highway's west side about 400 yards, cross the highway</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.393570" lon="-122.001400"><ele>954.8</ele><name>McKenzie River Trail summer parking (Santiam Wagon Road sign)</name><desc>source: start of USFS trails 3535 and 3507; OSM 'Santiam Wagon Road' information board node 7848225081 within 30 m; confidence: high; pdf_page: 246; book_elev_ft: 3100; quote: locate the summer parking lot for the McKenzie River Trail (to Clear Lake)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.399620" lon="-121.952190"><ele>1255.8</ele><name>Road 2676 junction</name><desc>source: east end of USFS trail 3535 SANTIAM WAGON ROAD EAST, on USFS road 2676000 (ENO), where 2676 turns north to Little Nash; confidence: high; pdf_page: 247; book_elev_ft: 4080; quote: along the twisting route 3.4 miles and a thousand vertical feet to a junction with Road 2676, a snowmobile route coming south from Little Nash Sno-Park 2.4 miles north</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Old Santiam Wagon Road</name><desc>1. Ikenick (Isaac Nickerson) Sno-Park -&gt; Leave the Prairie View east leg: usfs-trail (high), 1.73 mi | 2. Leave the Prairie View east leg -&gt; Primitive road (USFS 2600726): straight (medium), 0.24 mi | 3. Primitive road (USFS 2600726) -&gt; Fish Lake (north end of road 2600726): usfs-road (high), 0.37 mi | 4. Fish Lake (north end of road 2600726) -&gt; Highway crossing: straight (medium), 0.17 mi | 5. Highway crossing -&gt; McKenzie River Trail summer parking (Santiam Wagon Road sign): usfs-road (high), 0.10 mi | 6. McKenzie River Trail summer parking (Santiam Wagon Road sign) -&gt; Road 2676 junction: usfs-trail (high), 2.99 mi</desc>
